# Sarvasiksha AI

Personal voice/assistant API (Spring Boot) for Alexa and other clients.

## REST API

| Method | Path | Purpose |
|--------|------|---------|
| GET | `/api/v1/health` | Liveness + whether OpenAI key is configured |
| POST | `/api/v1/ask` | Ask assistant (simple JSON) |
| POST | `/alexa` | Alexa Custom Skill endpoint |

Alexa setup: `docs/alexa-setup.md`.

### Ask example

```bash
export OPENAI_API_KEY='your-key'   # never commit this
java -jar target/sarvashiksha-ai-0.0.1-SNAPSHOT.jar --server.port=8090

curl -sS -X POST http://localhost:8090/api/v1/ask \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
  -d '{"question":"What is photosynthesis?","locale":"en-IN"}'
```

## Local run

```bash
export OPENAI_API_KEY=...
mvn -DskipTests package
java -jar target/sarvashiksha-ai-0.0.1-SNAPSHOT.jar --server.port=8090
```

Or: `./scripts/run-local.sh /path/to/.crds`

## Render

- Build: `mvn -DskipTests package`
- Start: `java -jar target/sarvashiksha-ai-0.0.1-SNAPSHOT.jar`
- Env: `OPENAI_API_KEY` (required), optional `OPENAI_MODEL`, `SERVER_PORT` (Render sets `PORT` — map if needed)

## Security

- OpenAI key via `OPENAI_API_KEY` only; never commit keys.
- `.env` / `*.crds` are gitignored.
